& [InputContract] is strict
  + [kind] is directory or regular_file
  + [attributes] is an exact u32
  + [directory_case_sensitive_flags] is required and zero for directory, absent for regular_file
  + [component] is exact nonempty Unicode
  + [maximum_component_utf16_units] is 1 through 32767
  = must: reject unknown serialized fields, unknown enum variants, invalid limits, and incoherent kind-field relations

& [AttributeContract] is exhaustive
  + [READONLY] is 0x00000001
  + [HIDDEN] is 0x00000002
  + [SYSTEM] is 0x00000004
  + [DIRECTORY] is 0x00000010
  + [ARCHIVE] is 0x00000020
  + [NORMAL] is 0x00000080
  + [NOT_CONTENT_INDEXED] is 0x00002000
  + [benign_mask] is 0x00002027
  + [directory_allowed_mask] is 0x00002037
  + [directory] requires DIRECTORY and permits only directory_allowed_mask
  + [regular_normal] is exactly NORMAL
  + [regular_marked] is a nonzero subset of benign_mask
  + [everything_else] rejects as attribute fault

& [ComponentContract] is exact
  + [UTF16_units] are nonzero and do not exceed the supplied bound
  + [forbidden_scalars] are NUL, U+0001 through U+001F, less-than, greater-than, colon, quote, slash, backslash, vertical-bar, question-mark, and asterisk
  + [terminal] space and period reject
  + [navigation] dot and dot-dot reject
  + [Git_control] .git rejects by ordinal ASCII case-insensitive equality
  + [reserved_fixed] CON, PRN, AUX, and NUL reject before the first period
  + [reserved_numbered] COM1 through COM9 and LPT1 through LPT9 reject before the first period
  + [reserved_superscript] COM or LPT followed by superscript one, two, or three reject before the first period
  + [Unicode] is preserved without normalization

& [OutputContract] is inspectable
  + [decision] preserves exact input profile, kind, attributes, component, and case fields
  + [order_key_hex] is canonical lowercase hexadecimal encoding of exact component UTF-8 bytes
  + [fault] exposes one closed code, field, and bounded deterministic reason
  - never: output an OS, path, handle, Git, stream, receipt, same-handle, freshness, trust, or physical fact

& [ImplementationBoundary] is zero effect
  + [authorized_file] is crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/windows_entry_policy.rs
  + [authorized_export] is the exact library-module export
  + [authorized_tests] are focused unit, strict serialization, static no-effect, evidence, and workspace regression tests
  + [Cargo_delta] is zero
  + [lockfile_delta] is zero
  + [unsafe] is denied
  + [production_module_imports] are only std, serde, and this crate's pure forms
  - never: use windows-sys, filesystem, process, environment, clock, random, network, model, persistence, traversal, stream query, Git, receipt, mutation, seal, or promotion APIs

& [RequirementSet] is M2B-WEP-001 through M2B-WEP-014
  + [policy_requirements] are strict input, exhaustive attributes, exact case relation, bounded components, namespace rejection, exact Unicode, order bytes, closed faults, and zero effects
  + [correction_requirements] are historical supersession and unchanged-implementation revalidation

& [AcceptanceContract] is exact
  + [source] both manifests match exact bytes and SHA-256
  + [focused] nine unit tests and one independent static test pass in debug and overflow-checked release
  + [module] SHA-256 remains 19AD251C59F313F74B159D5D68A59A6861E799DF5ACC7E19F93B226ED43EA0CD
  + [effects] Cargo, lockfile, dependency, unsafe, and runtime-effect deltas remain zero
  + [evidence] manifest names the replacement signature and rehashes current artifacts
  + [global] workspace debug and release tests, format, warnings-denied lint, release build, warnings-denied docs, and audit pass
  + [dependency_gate] supplied entry-observation assembly remains unprocessed until this acceptance is recorded

& [AuthorityBoundary] is replacement and revalidation only
  + [allowed] unchanged pure module, export, tests, evidence, solution, proof, review, narrative, and dependent-policy citation after revalidation
  + [forbidden] production behavior change, profile change, dependency change, unsafe, physical observation, Win32, filesystem, traversal, stream query, Git reconciliation, receipt, admission, mutation, seal, or promotion

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is complete
  + [source_preserved] is original source and correction source with exact manifests
  + [delineated] is pure policy versus acquisition, provenance, and downstream effects
  + [exploded] is fourteen requirements, twelve constraints, twelve failures, and ten verification gates
  + [semantically_refined] is policy, admitted, exact, and valid-signature meaning
  + [constraint_checked] is source, framework protocol, artifact guard, and byte-identical implementation
  + [pruned] is false protocol authority, retroactive authorization, semantic drift, and physical overclaim
  + [data_design_checked] is one closed input-to-decision-or-fault transform
  + [seven_fold_phase_locked] is subject, terms, data, relations, constraints, failures, and proof convergence
  + [justified] is truthful supersession with support, confidence, counterargument, residual risk, invalidation, and rollback
  + [planned] is ordered preservation, processing, signing, revalidation, evidence, proof, and publication
  + [registry_recorded] is graph-addressable source, correction, signature, implementation, evidence, and dependency lineage

